   110	from a working tree where untrusted PR-head content has been checked out (e.g. after a manual
   111	`gh pr checkout`). BB fetches PR data via `gh api` (diff-as-data) and never writes PR files to the
   112	working tree, so the reviewed diff is safe; but `.loa.config.yaml` (models, budgets,
   113	`cross_repo.allowed_owners`, `cross_repo.manual_refs`) is read from the **local checkout**, which
   114	must therefore be trusted. The auto-detected cross-repo allowlist defaults to the reviewed PR's own
   115	org (derived from PR metadata, independent of config); `allowed_owners` / `manual_refs` only widen
   116	that and assume a trusted config source. Investigated + closed as not-applicable in the shipped
   117	invocation model (no PR-head checkout) — see #1050. Since cycle-129 the provider, locality and
   118	exit keys follow the trusted-source precedence below even when the checkout is a PR head.
   119	
   120	## Self-Review Opt-In (#796 / vision-013)
   121	
   122	When BB reviews a PR that modifies BB itself — or any other framework file under `.claude/`, `grimoires/`, `.beads/`, etc. — the Loa-aware filter normally strips those files from the review payload before the multi-model pass. This is correct for code-PR reviews (no review noise from grimoire side-effects) but inverts on self-modifying PRs (the framework files ARE the substance).
